.TH NAP 1 "2026" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nap \- power, lid and UPS management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nap
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nap
reports power state and controls systemd-inhibit locks, the lid switch
action, the hardware battery charge limit, dark mode, and battery-triggered
UPS shutdown. Exit status is 0 on success and 1 on any error; \fBnap stay\fR
returns the wrapped command's exit code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report batteries (status, percent, health percent, watts), AC adapters,
thermal zones, and the configured lid action from
.IR /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/90-chonkos-lid.conf .
.TP
.BR stay " " DURATION
Hold a systemd-inhibit lock (idle:sleep:handle-lid-switch, mode block) for
DURATION, e.g. 90s, 45m, 1h30m. DURATION must be positive.
.TP
.BR stay " \-\- " COMMAND " [ARG...]"
Hold the inhibitor lock until COMMAND exits; the exit code of nap is the
exit code of COMMAND (128+signal if killed). With \fB\-\-json\fR the child's
stdout is redirected to stderr and nap prints {"exit_code": N}.
.TP
.BR lid " status"
Print the current lid drop-in contents.
.TP
.BR lid " sleep"
Set HandleLidSwitch and HandleLidSwitchExternalPower to suspend. Requires
root. Never restarts systemd-logind; only runs
.BR "systemctl reload systemd-logind" .
.TP
.BR lid " ignore"
Set both lid actions to ignore. Requires root; same reload behavior.
.TP
.BR guard " enable [\fB\-\-limit\fR 60|80]"
Set a hardware battery charge limit (default 60) and persist it in a TLP
drop-in. IdeaPad/Legion models with the ideapad_acpi binary conservation
switch use the factory limit for either option; ThinkPad and other models
use charge_control_end_threshold (with charge_control_start_threshold).
Requires root.
.TP
.BR guard " disable"
Remove the hardware charge limit and the TLP drop-in. Requires root.
.TP
.BR guard " status"
Report the detected interface, current settings, the TLP drop-in and the
maximum thermal-zone temperature.
.TP
.BR dark " on"
Switch off panel backlights, request TTY blanking after one minute and
disable Wi-Fi power saving where supported; reports before/after battery
power readings when available. Requires root.
.TP
.BR dark " off"
Restore the backlights and remove the NetworkManager drop-in. Requires root.
.TP
.BR dark " status"
Show current panel, console and drop-in state.
.TP
.BR dive " enable [\fB\-\-threshold\fR 10..50] [\fB\-\-services\fR a.service,b.service]"
Configure battery-triggered UPS shutdown, persisted under /var/lib/chonkos/;
also creates /var/lib/chonkos/nap-dive.enabled, which arms the
udev-triggered chonkos-nap-dive.service. Default threshold 20. Requires
root. With \fB\-\-json\fR prints
{"status":"enabled","config":{"threshold_percent":20,"services":[...]}}.
.TP
.BR dive " disable"
Remove the UPS configuration and the enabled marker. Requires root.
.TP
.BR dive " status"
Report the UPS configuration.
.TP
.BR dive " \fB\-\-event\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]"
Run the UPS check (invoked by chonkos-nap-dive.service on power_supply
change events). Reports ac_online or no_battery when not discharging;
on_battery_monitoring while above the threshold; at or below the threshold
it marks a \fBpowerloss\fR seal, stops the configured services, syncs and
powers off (\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR only lists the steps). The poweroff requires
root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
nap status
.TP
nap --json status
.TP
nap stay 1h30m
.TP
nap stay -- make -j4
.TP
nap lid status
.TP
sudo nap lid ignore
.TP
sudo nap guard enable --limit 80
.TP
nap guard status
.TP
sudo nap dark on
.TP
nap --json dark status
.TP
sudo nap dive enable --threshold 20 --services docker.service
.TP
sudo nap dive --event --dry-run
.TP
sudo nap --json dive --event
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/90-chonkos-lid.conf
ChonkOS logind lid drop-in written by \fBnap lid\fR.
.TP
.I /var/lib/chonkos/nap-dive.enabled
Marker arming the udev-triggered chonkos-nap-dive.service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chonk (1),
.BR whisker (1)
